name issue_346_reconfigure_cross_join
describe issue_204_cross_traffic_join with quality scaling on: link loss after 2 Mbps cross traffic joins at 10 s, just after the 540p switch (#346)
# sm_compare runs 80 seeds here (#408). Both stacks enter the stuck mode of #390 (cuts end above the free 1 Mbps,
# the queue stays full, about 10 freezes) on about 2.5 % of seeds, depending on the RTCP phase at the join: libwebrtc
# 10 of 400 seed-runs over five RTCPSender schedules (#397), ours 3 of 80 on main d02f90f (seeds 5, 74, 75; mean 2.99
# freezes). On 10 seeds one stuck draw moves the mean by about 0.9 freezes and decides the cell, as seed 5 did after #378.
compare_seeds 80
duration 40s
quality_scaling on
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=40ms queue=300ms
at 10s cross=2000kbps
at 25s cross=0kbps
# libwebrtc seeds 1-3 (#344's compare-webrtc @ 3d46b11): loss 0.39/0.32/0.33 %. main before #346: 0.71/0.55/0.65 %.
# With the port, seeds 1-5: 0.38/0.53/0.21/0.39/2.04 %. On seed 5 the scaler goes up to 720p at 13 s, while the
# cross traffic holds the target near 1 Mbps (libwebrtc's seed 3 also switches to 720p at 13 s); that is a scaler
# decision, not this item's reset, so this copy is coverage for the flip and its line holds on every seed.
# Judge the family on compare-webrtc's 10 seeds.
expect net.loss_pct < 2.5
